            <ArticleTitle>[Significance of C-reactive protein in asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>472-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>C-reactive protein (CPR) has been showed to be a specific and sensitive marker in diagnosing and monitoring of many inflammatory diseases. High-sensitive CRP is also a useful diagnostic tool to asses subclinical systemic inflammation in circulatory system diseases and diabetes. There is increasing evidence confirming the presence of systemic inflammation in asthma and the possibility of using hs-CRP in diagnosis and treatment monitoring of this disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
